  "published": "2026-08-24",
  "insights": [
   "Inflation expectations are at most modestly elevated and not at immediate risk of unanchoring despite five years of above-target inflation.",
   "Long-term household inflation expectations have returned to levels seen in the mid-2000s, while short-term expectations remain somewhat elevated due to this year's oil shock.",
   "Monetary policy has a limited role in anchoring expectations because households and firms are largely inattentive to the Fed unless inflation is very high.",
   "The Fed's communication and credibility alone are unlikely to anchor expectations; a sustained decline in realized inflation is the primary driver.",
   "A memory-based model suggests that the net effect of the last two cycles (low inflation followed by high inflation) has left expectations only slightly above a 2% counterfactual.",
   "Attentiveness to inflation, measured by 'Don't Know' responses in surveys, has normalized to pre-pandemic levels.",
   "The bank forecasts a return to target inflation by the end of 2027 as oil prices stabilize and tariff effects fade."
